                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "i first played \"Always Remember Me\" when i was only 11 or 12 years old, and somehow, all these years later, this little game still holds such a warm and special place in my heart.\r\n\r\nthere is something incredibly comforting about it. the atmosphere, the characters, the story and everything feels strangely familiar, almost like returning to a place you haven’t visited in years but somehow still remember perfectly. the characters have stayed with me for so long that they feel almost like old friends, or little pieces of my childhood that i never really had to say goodbye to.\r\n\r\nand the soundtrack… i don’t think i can properly put into words what it means to me. some melodies simply stay in your heart, even when years pass and you grow into a completely different person. every time i hear it, it brings back that very specific warmth and nostalgia i felt playing this game as a child.\r\n\r\n\"Always Remember Me\" may not be the most technically impressive or modern game, but i don’t think that matters. it became one of those rare experiences that quietly grows with you and remains precious simply because of how it made you feel.\r\n\r\nit has been so many years, and i still remember it with so much tenderness. some games you play and forget. others become a small part of you.\r\n\r\nthis one became a little part of my heart! ♡",
